<TEXT IntroTextCTD none 0>
<TITLE To Curse the Darkness>
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
You have stopped briefly in the small medieval village of Temesvar for a brief respite on your way through the wilder lands that cover most of this area. Not too soon, either, as the bone-chilling howls you heard during the night's trek revealed the presence of predatory Lupines within these mountains. Lupines who hate Cainites. 
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
The village consists of little more than an Inn, church, and graveyard, along with the simple cottages of the residents. Still, it should serve as safe haven for a few nights before venturing forth into the dangerous forests. The entire village is protected by a stone wall and a small group of men-at-arms. 
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
The coterie has chosen to visit the small Inn within the gates of the village, the Mossy Hearth, to hear of the local gossip, and possibly learn of any signs indicating resident Cainites. The townspeople are wary of strangers, so you chose a table in a shadowed corner to feign drinking the modest beer offered by the burly barkeep. The worried conversation in the Inn touches upon several topics, including a recent fire and a wasting sickness that has spread across the village... 
</TEXT>

<TEXT LeComteLetter none 0>
<TITLE LeComte's Letter>
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Master Thelonius-
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
I have a matter of great import to discuss. Meet me at the empty cottage near the church this evening at midnight. Tell no one of the meeting, as I suspect treachery amongst your brood.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Le Comte
</TEXT>

<TEXT TheloniusJournal none 0>
<TITLE Thelonius' Journal>
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
January the 23rd
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Delivered 'The Last Caress' painting to Le Comte. What secrets he is attempting the glean from the painting I do not know, but he has paid handsomely in gold and shared some pearls of his artistic wisdom with me. He has a keen eye, and could help me with my skull sculptures. 
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
March the 12th
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Damn the worm! Discovered Melmoth's treachery and his invasion of my Chamber. It is unknown how he managed entry, as none of the others can access it save myself. Took mercy and did not stake him out in the sun. Expelled him from the haven. A great loss, as no one of us had mastered the art of Obfuscation like Melmoth.. His downfall was his use of the hidden arts to sneak and steal from his own Clan.
</TEXT>

<TEXT Narrator_15_1_560 Narrator_15_1_560.mp3 0>
<TITLE The Chronicle of Caine>
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
In the beginning there was only Caine.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Caine who sacrificed his brother out of love.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Caine who was cast out.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Caine who was cursed with the lust for blood.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
It is Caine from whom we all come,
Our sire's sire.
</TEXT>

<TEXT Narrator_15_1_561 Narrator_15_1_561.mp3 0>
<TITLE The Chronicle of Caine>
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
For the passing of an age Caine lived in the land of Nod,
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
In loneliness and suffering.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
For an eon he remained alone.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
But the passing of memory drowned his sorrow.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
And so he returned to the world of mortals,
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
To the world of mortals,
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
To the world his brother and his brother's children had created.
</TEXT>

<TEXT Narrator_15_1_562 Narrator_15_1_562.mp3 0>
<TITLE The Chronicle of Caine>
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Though he became ruler of a mighty nation, Caine was still alone,
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
For none was as he. His sorrow grew once again.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Then he committed another great sin, for he begat progeny,
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Of whom there were only three.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
But from them came more progeny, Caine’s grandchilder,
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
And then Caine said, "An end to this crime. There shall be no more."
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
And as Caine’s word was law, his brood obeyed him.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
The city stood for many ages,
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
And became the center of a mighty empire.
</TEXT>

<TEXT Narrator_15_1_563 Narrator_15_1_563.mp3 0>
<TITLE The Chronicle of Caine>
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
But then came the Deluge, a Great Flood that washed over the world.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
The city was destroyed,
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
And its people along with it.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Again Caine fell into a great sorrow and went into solitude,
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Becoming as a dog amidst the wastes,
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
And leaving his progeny to their own ends.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
They came to him and begged him to return,
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
To help them rebuild the city.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
But he would not come with them,
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Saying the Flood had been sent as punishment
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
For his having returned to the world of life
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
And subverting the true law.
</TEXT>

<TEXT Narrator_15_1_564 Narrator_15_1_564.mp3 0>
<TITLE The Chronicle of Caine>
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
A great war was waged, the elders against their children,
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
And the children slew their parents.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
The rebels then built a new city
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
And brought to it 13 tribes.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
It was a beautiful city and its people worshipped them as gods.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
They created new progeny of their own,
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
The fourth generation of Cainites.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
But they feared the Jyhad,
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
And it was forbidden for those childer
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
To create others of their kind.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Although this city was as great as Caine’s, eventually it grew old.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
As do all living things, it slowly began to die.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Their city was destroyed and their power extinguished.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
With their authority gone, all were free to create their own broods,
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
And soon there were many new Cainites,
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Who ruled across the face of the Earth.
</TEXT>

<TEXT EndTextBadCTD none 0>
<TITLE Chronicle Completed>
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
After the fight, Melmoth became visible and his bony body clattered to the ground. The Monocle fell and shattered to pieces. From the shadows in the corner of the room, Rebecca approached, horribly disfigured from Melmoth's blood. Trembling, holding a dagger within her hands, she cried out and killed herself.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Ragwick entered the scene, too late to save his beloved Rebecca. If only you had kept the Monocle from Melmoth's clutches, you may have averted this horrible outcome!
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
The End.
</TEXT>

<TEXT EndTextGoodCTD none 0>
<TITLE Chronicle Completed>
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Melmoth has been destroyed, his fabulous Monocle is now in your possession! The young lovers have been reunited, and you may enlist their aid in traversing the forest to the west. Congratulations!
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
The End.
</TEXT>


